    <div class="container">
        <div class="header">
            <h1>Fitness Tracker User Health & Activity Analytics Report</h1>
            <p class="subtitle">A comprehensive analysis of daily health metrics, activity patterns, and lifestyle indicators across a synthetic cohort of fitness tracker users from 2015 to 2025.</p>
            <p class="meta">Dataset: 4,000 records | 970 unique users | Jan 2015 – Dec 2025 | Audience: Health Analytics Team</p>
        </div>

        <!-- KPI Summary -->
        <div class="kpi-grid">
            <div class="kpi-card">
                <h3>Average Daily Steps</h3>
                <div class="value">10,574</div>
                <div class="detail">Range: 1,003 – 19,993 | Median: 10,725</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-card green">
                <h3>Average Calories Burned</h3>
                <div class="value">617</div>
                <div class="detail">kcal per day</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-card orange">
                <h3>Average Sleep Duration</h3>
                <div class="value">6.99</div>
                <div class="detail">hours per night</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-card purple">
                <h3>Workout Participation Rate</h3>
                <div class="value">83.1%</div>
                <div class="detail">3,325 of 4,000 records</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-card red">
                <h3>Average Stress Level</h3>
                <div class="value">5.45</div>
                <div class="detail">Scale: 1 (low) – 10 (high)</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 1: Demographics -->
        <section id="demographic-overview">
            <h2>1. User Demographics & Body Metrics Overview</h2>
            <p>This section provides a foundational understanding of the user cohort's demographic composition and body metrics.</p>

            <h3>Gender Distribution</h3>
            <div class="stat-row">
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <label>Male</label>
                    <div class="number">50.6%</div>
                    <div>2,025 records</div>
                </div>
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <label>Female</label>
                    <div class="number">49.4%</div>
                    <div>1,975 records</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Age Distribution</h3>
            <p>The cohort spans ages 18–59 with a mean age of 38.5 years. Distribution across age groups is relatively balanced:</p>
            <table>
                <tr><th>Age Group</th><th>Avg Steps</th><th>Avg BMI</th><th>Record Count</th></tr>
                <tr><td>18–25</td><td>10,844</td><td>24.48</td><td>~800</td></tr>
                <tr><td>26–35</td><td>10,449</td><td>24.53</td><td>~800</td></tr>
                <tr><td>36–45</td><td>10,392</td><td>24.68</td><td>~800</td></tr>
                <tr><td>46–55</td><td>10,732</td><td>24.44</td><td>~800</td></tr>
                <tr><td>55+</td><td>10,481</td><td>25.06</td><td>~800</td></tr>
            </table>

            <h3>Body Metrics</h3>
            <div class="stat-row">
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <label>Average Height</label>
                    <div class="number">170.0 cm</div>
                    <div>Male: 169.9 cm | Female: 170.0 cm</div>
                </div>
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <label>Average Weight</label>
                    <div class="number">70.3 kg</div>
                    <div>Male: 70.3 kg | Female: 70.3 kg</div>
                </div>
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <label>Average BMI</label>
                    <div class="number">24.59</div>
                    <div>Healthy range (18.5–24.9)</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="chart-container full-width-chart">
                <h4>Steps Distribution</h4>
                <canvas id="stepsDistChart"></canvas>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 2: Activity Analysis -->
        <section id="activity-analysis">
            <h2>2. Physical Activity & Workout Patterns</h2>
            <p>Analysis of daily step counts, workout types, and workout durations across the user base.</p>

            <h3>Workout Type Distribution</h3>
            <p>Among the 83.1% of records with a workout, distribution across types is nearly even:</p>
            <table>
                <tr><th>Workout Type</th><th>Count</th><th>% of Workout Records</th><th>Avg Duration (min)</th></tr>
                <tr><td>Gym</td><td>689</td><td>20.7%</td><td>55.6</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Walking</td><td>676</td><td>20.3%</td><td>53.6</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Yoga</td><td>675</td><td>20.3%</td><td>54.5</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Cycling</td><td>644</td><td>19.4%</td><td>53.6</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Running</td><td>641</td><td>19.3%</td><td>55.0</td></tr>
            </table>

            <h3>Workout Participation by Demographic</h3>
            <div class="stat-row">
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <label>By Gender</label>
                    <div class="number">Male: 83.6% | Female: 82.7%</div>
                </div>
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <label>By Mood</label>
                    <div class="number">Happy: 82.9% | Neutral: 83.9% | Tired: 82.6%</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Steps by Workout Type</h3>
            <div class="chart-grid">
                <div class="chart-container">
                    <h4>Average Daily Steps by Workout Type</h4>
                    <canvas id="stepsByWorkoutChart"></canvas>
                </div>
                <div class="chart-container">
                    <h4>Calories Burned by Workout Type</h4>
                    <canvas id="calByWorkoutChart"></canvas>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="insight-box">
                <h4>Key Finding</h4>
                <p>Running yields the highest average daily steps (10,721) and calories burned (622 kcal), while Walking shows the lowest steps (10,353) despite similar workout durations.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 3: Health Vitals -->
        <section id="health-vitals">
            <h2>3. Heart Rate, Sleep & Calorie Burn Analysis</h2>
            <p>Examination of vital health metrics and their relationships with other factors.</p>

            <h3>Heart Rate</h3>
            <div class="stat-row">
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <label>Average Heart Rate</label>
                    <div class="number">75.1 bpm</div>
                </div>
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <label>Range</label>
                    <div class="number">50 – 110 bpm</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Sleep Analysis</h3>
            <p>Average sleep duration is 6.99 hours with minimal variation across stress levels and moods:</p>
            <table>
                <tr><th>Metric</th><th>Value</th></tr>
                <tr><td>Mean Sleep</td><td>6.99 hours</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Median Sleep</td><td>7.00 hours</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Min / Max</td><td>3.0 / 10.0 hours</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Sleep by Mood (Happy)</td><td>7.02 hours</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Sleep by Mood (Neutral)</td><td>7.01 hours</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Sleep by Mood (Tired)</td><td>6.95 hours</td></tr>
            </table>

            <h3>Calorie Burn Patterns</h3>
            <div class="stat-row">
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <label>Daily Average</label>
                    <div class="number">617 kcal</div>
                </div>
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <label>Correlation with Steps</label>
                    <div class="number">r = 0.973</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="chart-container full-width-chart">
                <h4>Heart Rate Distribution by Age Group</h4>
                <canvas id="heartRateChart"></canvas>
            </div>

            <div class="insight-box">
                <h4>Key Finding</h4>
                <p>Sleep duration shows negligible correlation with activity levels (r = 0.022) and stress (r = -0.008). This suggests daily sleep is largely independent of physical activity and stress in this cohort.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 4: Lifestyle Wellness -->
        <section id="lifestyle-wellness">
            <h2>4. Lifestyle & Wellness Indicators</h2>
            <p>Assessment of water intake, stress levels, and mood distributions.</p>

            <h3>Stress Level Distribution</h3>
            <p>Stress levels are uniformly distributed across the 1–10 scale, with slight peaks at levels 1–2:</p>
            <div class="chart-container full-width-chart">
                <h4>Stress Level Distribution</h4>
                <canvas id="stressDistChart"></canvas>
            </div>

            <h3>Water Intake</h3>
            <div class="stat-row">
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <label>Daily Average</label>
                    <div class="number">2.49 L</div>
                </div>
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <label>Range</label>
                    <div class="number">0.50 – 5.00 L</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Mood Distribution</h3>
            <div class="chart-grid">
                <div class="chart-container">
                    <h4>Mood Distribution</h4>
                    <canvas id="moodDistChart"></canvas>
                </div>
                <div class="chart-container">
                    <h4>Mood by Workout Type</h4>
                    <canvas id="moodByWorkoutChart"></canvas>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="insight-box">
                <h4>Key Finding</h4>
                <p>Stress shows virtually no correlation with activity levels (r = -0.012) or sleep (r = -0.008). Higher activity quartiles report slightly lower stress (Q4: 5.34 vs Q1: 5.47), but the effect is marginal.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 5: Temporal Trends -->
        <section id="temporal-trends">
            <h2>5. Temporal Trends & Seasonal Patterns</h2>
            <p>Investigation of how key health and activity metrics evolve over time.</p>

            <div class="insight-box" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fef3c7 0%, #fde68a 100%); border-left-color: #f9ab00;">
                <h4 style="color: #92400e;">Priority Section</h4>
                <p>This section receives extra attention as it directly informs roadmap timing decisions.</p>
            </div>

            <h3>Year-over-Year Trends (2015–2025)</h3>
            <div class="chart-container full-width-chart">
                <h4>Average Daily Steps by Year</h4>
                <canvas id="yearlyStepsChart"></canvas>
            </div>

            <table>
                <tr><th>Year</th><th>Avg Steps</th><th>YoY Change</th><th>Avg Calories</th><th>Workout Rate</th></tr>
                <tr><td>2015</td><td>10,963</td><td>—</td><td>632</td><td>84.4%</td></tr>
                <tr><td>2016</td><td>11,105</td><td>+1.3%</td><td>640</td><td>83.6%</td></tr>
                <tr><td>2017</td><td>10,574</td><td>-4.8%</td><td>617</td><td>84.1%</td></tr>
                <tr><td>2018</td><td>10,003</td><td>-5.4%</td><td>598</td><td>77.5%</td></tr>
                <tr><td>2019</td><td>10,909</td><td>+9.1%</td><td>628</td><td>86.6%</td></tr>
                <tr><td>2020</td><td>10,335</td><td>-5.3%</td><td>606</td><td>82.2%</td></tr>
                <tr><td>2021</td><td>10,425</td><td>+0.9%</td><td>609</td><td>80.0%</td></tr>
                <tr><td>2022</td><td>10,390</td><td>-0.3%</td><td>612</td><td>85.2%</td></tr>
                <tr><td>2023</td><td>10,742</td><td>+3.4%</td><td>621</td><td>83.8%</td></tr>
                <tr><td>2024</td><td>10,582</td><td>-1.5%</td><td>618</td><td>81.4%</td></tr>
                <tr><td>2025*</td><td>10,271</td><td>-2.9%</td><td>601</td><td>85.6%</td></tr>
            </table>
            <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: #888;">*2025 data partial (through Dec 13)</p>

            <h3>Monthly Seasonal Patterns</h3>
            <div class="chart-container full-width-chart">
                <h4>Monthly Average Steps (All Years Combined)</h4>
                <canvas id="monthlyStepsChart"></canvas>
